# Triaged Trivy exceptions for the api and worker images.
#
# Every line here suppresses one HIGH/CRITICAL finding that Trivy would otherwise
# fail the build on, so keep the list short: each entry carries a reason and a
# review-by date, and an exception that outlives its reason is a bug. When Debian
# ships a fix, bump the base image digest and delete the entry.
#
# Base image: python:3.12-slim (Debian 13.7 / trixie), digest
#   sha256:a6e34c598f2467ed0e9a8d349809fcd8b5c603269512df273a0bb1784edc11b1
# which was already the latest 3.12 slim tag as of 2026-10-15. Trivy reports no
# fixed version for any of the CVEs below, so the strict HIGH/CRITICAL gate
# cannot pass without them. Re-review the whole file by 2027-01-01.

CVE-2025-69720  # python:3.12-slim base (Debian): ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin); HIGH; no fixed version as of 2026-10-15; base is latest digest; review by 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-9538   # python:3.12-slim base (Debian): perl (perl-base); HIGH; no fixed version as of 2026-10-15; base is latest digest; review by 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-16742  # python:3.12-slim base (Debian): systemd (libsystemd0, libudev1); HIGH; no fixed version as of 2026-10-15; base is latest digest; review by 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-54369  # python:3.12-slim base (Debian): acl (libacl1); HIGH; no fixed version as of 2026-10-15; base is latest digest; review by 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-76642  # python:3.12-slim base (Debian): util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux); HIGH; no fixed version as of 2026-10-15; base is latest digest; review by 2027-01-01
